==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|dah}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þaką}}; compare Low German {{m|nds|Dack}}, Dutch {{m|nl|dak}}, English {{m|en|thack}}, {{m|en|thatch}}, Danish {{m|da|tag}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*teg-}}, and akin to Latin {{m|la|toga||garment}} and Ancient Greek {{m|grc|στέγος||roof}}.

